---
title: Frequently Asked Questions | Thomas Web Group
description: Answers to common questions about website design, search visibility, social media, CRM systems, automation, and working with Thomas Web Group.
layout: 'base.njk'
permalink: /faq/
---

<main class="main">
  <section id="faq" class="portfolio-details section">
    <div class="container section-title" data-aos="fade-up">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div><span>Websites, Marketing,</span> <span class="description-title">and Business Systems</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
      <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-10">
          <div class="portfolio-details-content">
            <div class="project-overview">
              <h1>Questions About Working With Us</h1>
              <div class="accordion project-accordion" id="fullFaq">
                {% set questions = [
                  ['What services does Thomas Web Group offer?', 'We help small businesses with websites, Google and AI search visibility, social media, customer and lead management, automation, system integrations, and reporting. Services can be combined based on your business needs.'],
                  ['Can you improve a website I already have?', 'Yes. We can review your current website and discuss improvements or a redesign. The right approach depends on how the existing site is built and what you want it to accomplish.'],
                  ['Do you help businesses appear on Google and AI search tools?', 'We can improve the content, structure, and technical foundations that help search engines and AI-powered tools understand your business. These efforts support discoverability, but no provider can guarantee specific rankings or recommendations.'],
                  ['Can you help with HubSpot or another CRM?', 'Yes. We work with customer management systems, including HubSpot, to help organize information, track opportunities, automate follow-up, and connect business tools.'],
                  ['Do you offer ongoing support?', 'Yes. Depending on the project, ongoing work may include website updates, social media management, CRM administration, automation, or reporting. The specific responsibilities are agreed upon before work begins.'],
                  ['How much do your services cost?', "Project pricing depends on the work involved. Tell us what you need, and we'll discuss an appropriate scope and quote."],
                  ['Do you only work with businesses in East Tennessee?', 'East Tennessee is our local market, but many website, CRM, marketing, and automation projects can be handled remotely.'],
                  ['What happens after I submit a project inquiry?', "We'll review the information you've provided and follow up to discuss your business, what you're trying to accomplish, and the potential next steps."]
                ] %}
                {% for item in questions %}
                <div class="accordion-item" data-aos="fade-up">
                  <h2 class="accordion-header" id="full-faq-heading-{{ loop.index }}">
                    <button class="accordion-button {% if not loop.first %}collapsed{% endif %}" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#full-faq-{{ loop.index }}" aria-expanded="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}" aria-controls="full-faq-{{ loop.index }}"><i class="bi bi-question-circle me-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ item[0] }}</button>
                  </h2>
                  <div id="full-faq-{{ loop.index }}" class="accordion-collapse collapse {% if loop.first %}show{% endif %}" data-bs-parent="#fullFaq">
                    <div class="accordion-body"><p>{{ item[1] }}</p></div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
              <div class="text-center mt-5">
                <h2>Still Have Questions About Your Project?</h2>
                <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Get a Project Quote</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
